From 562deca3450ff2a7675efe4e3bc69d11a06e4ef0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:26:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): permit exactly attested SSH pool requirements
 [daveey]

Why: scoped pickup recovery could not move a card requiring ssh:mini off a
shutdown-held worker even though another worker carried the operator label.
Core deliberately excluded SSH because Board selection lacked its mapping.
Board PR148 is now merged/deployed at 7ddd9fd5710061d69d558722e5044df7d755ea42;
live isolated reserve probes recognize mini/mbp and reject ssh:other.

Enable only ssh:mini and ssh:mbp in the existing core Board allowlist.
Preserve per-host operator attestation, freshness/hold/claim fences and task
requirements through the real scoped alarm move. Remove test monkeypatching
that concealed the production contract. Document access revocation and the
difference between structural queue admission and execution eligibility.

Proof:
- Canonical runner: 20 consumer/docs files, 1118 passed, 0 failed.
- Removing either SSH entry: three targeted failures per mutant, including
  the corresponding real alarm move; source restored after each.
- Read-only hub allowlist-delta replay: 29840 rows, 70 changed replicas of
  51 distinct tasks, all explicitly declaring mini/mbp (includes history
  and archived fixtures). This is contract replay, not claim eligibility.
- Board live probe fixtures archived and read back; worker-2 hold retained.
- No requirement edits, worker restarts, CI implementation edits or spend.
